  m_Name: Blade9
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade9
  description: The Blade9 is a tiny, elongated blade situated at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, constructed from Blades texture material, responsible for
    directing and accelerating the airflow through the engine, with a notable aspect
    being its unique texture that enhances its aerodynamic properties. Its elongated
    shape allows for a larger surface area, increasing its ability to transfer energy
    to the air. As a key component of the compressor stage, Blade9 contributes significantly
    to the engine's ability to generate thrust.
